  "textureNote": "Aliases copy settlement-mud-v1's rows for the same archive-absent Creation Club, resource-pack and Dragonborn textures; desertcracked02 takes its desertcracked01 sibling's stand-in. boneflute01 is left out: its only diffuse is a Creation Club weapon texture (bgssse001 fangofhaynekhtnamet) absent from the vault, so the flute stays a named no-kit-asset gap in the bundle. Walk 3 lane L14: telwoodendoor01 (the Hist trunk's bark) takes dungeon-root-v1's stand-in; 22 more pieces the Murkmire cells reference are left out on the boneflute's rule, each because a diffuse it needs sits only in an archive the vault lacks (Creation Club bgssse001/bgssse037/bgssse025 fish, rods, weapons and ingredients; the AE _ResourcePack palm, snow-gum and willow trees; _byoh food; Dragonborn dlc2darkelffurniture01 and telinsideblob01; a Curse of Immortals turtle shell): boneflute01, doll_turtle, marshmerrowstew, saltricenoodles, crateopen01, ctq_treepalm03-05, jungletree04-06, histgland03, rainforesttree02, willow03-04, argonianspearsquiver, the three mounted fish, redwort01, argbonedagger, argknife. Walk 5: the AE _ResourcePack ceramic01teal_d (the Murkmire shells' teal-glazed inner walls) and baldcypressbark01_d (the rustic furniture and firewood) exist in the vault only as King of the Murkmire's own 256 px LOD copies under textures/lod/, the same picture at distance resolution; the two aliases name those copies explicitly, since the stem fallback no longer takes a LOD texture.",
